### 2.5 Webhook Events

Webhooks are important for team adoption and integrations.

#### Recommended events

- `prompt.created`
- `prompt.updated`
- `prompt.deleted`
- `prompt.version.created`
- `prompt.tagged`
- `prompt.untagged`
- `workspace.member_added`
- `workspace.member_removed`
- `import.completed`
- `export.completed`

#### Webhook design rules

- Send event id, event type, created time, workspace id, and resource payload.
- Deliver events asynchronously.
- Retry on transient failures.
- Sign webhook payloads with an HMAC signature.
- Include idempotency/event IDs so receivers can dedupe.

#### Delivery guarantees

- At-least-once delivery
- Document that duplicates may occur
- Provide retry and dead-letter logging

